    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I've been noticing that even when I keep the temperature somewhat steady, the activity feels almost... unpredictable? Like, it goes from totally dormant to aggressively active overnight. Is there a specific threshold where the Lactobacillus starts outcompeting the yeast, or is it more about the specific enzymes breaking down the starches in the flour? I'm trying to understand if there's a way to \"tame\" that volatility so it doesn't feel so erratic.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
