      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The unpredictability you feel is likely a kinetic effect of yeast becoming dormant in cooler conditions while lactobacilli remain metabolically active, leading to a pH spike before the yeast reawakens. Lactobacilli will formally outcompete yeast for space and oxygen when acidity rises above roughly pH 3.5, signaling the need for more frequent feeding rather than switching to high-protein flours. To tame this volatility, try a long river method with consistent feedings to build a more robust, stable culture. Experimenting with slightly lower reciprocation frequency (less feeding) and ensuring your setup is airtight can help prevent die-offs that cause erratic swings.",
